For every lambda term and every environment, applying the raw fixed point first to the encoding of the term and then to the environment yields the interpretation of the term at that environment.

Induct on the term. A variable rewrites by the double application and the tag-zero step. Zero rewrites by the tag-one step. Successor and predecessor rewrite by the tag-two and tag-three steps, simplify the payload and the tag injection, and use the inductive hypothesis. A conditional rewrites by the tag-four step and the four sequence projections, then uses the four inductive hypotheses. An application rewrites by the tag-five step and the two sequence projections, then uses both inductive hypotheses. An abstraction rewrites by the tag-six step and the environment update at a numeral, and congruence of the graph uses the inductive hypothesis on the body.
